From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 03:07:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: coda: add the Sophgo SG2000 JPEG unit

The SG2000 has a standalone Chips&Media JPEG unit (JPU). It has the
registers of the CODA960 JPEG engine, at offset 0 instead of 0x3000, and
no BIT processor and no firmware.

The CODA960 JPEG engine gets the source frame through the CODA's GDI. The
JPU takes the frame addresses and strides in its own registers, and the
CbCr interleave value 2 for NV12.

Support the JPEG encoder. Reset the JPU with its INIT command, where the
CODA960 resets the whole CODA. After a timeout, also pulse the reset
line: after a stalled frame, INIT leaves state behind and the next frame
has wrong DC predictions. Give the JPU its own debugfs directory.

The register sequence follows Sophgo's vendor driver.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
